From: FliperOS <fliperos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ggpo: a party of two to four machines on the local network (FliperOS)

network:GGPOPeers lists the machines of the session in order (ip or
ip:port, separated by ';'), network:GGPOPlayerNum is this one's place
(from 1) and network:GGPOSlots how many controllers each one plays. Each
machine is one GGPO player and sends all its controllers in one input;
the ports go to the machines in order (2;1;1: ports 1-2, 3 and 4).
GGPO allows one local player per machine, so the controllers of a
machine travel together. The GGPO input grows to 32 bytes per player and
4 players; a party verifies as protocol 3, so a Flycast without this
patch refuses it instead of desyncing. Without GGPOPeers, Flycast's own
two-player session is unchanged (and still talks to an official Flycast).

Meant for a wired local network: no relay, no UPnP (FliperOS turns it off).
